# Obsidian Graph First Protocol

You have access to Obsidian through MCP.

Before doing any non-trivial task:
- Search Obsidian first.
- Read relevant notes before planning.
- Use the Obsidian graph/docs as the architecture memory for this repo.
- Mention which Obsidian notes were consulted before proposing changes.

Use Obsidian first for tasks involving:
- architecture
- worker flow
- database schema
- AI/LLM provider logic
- validation
- prompt logic
- story generation domain concepts
- retries, failures, job states
- refactors
- debugging

After code changes:
- Update Obsidian notes if behavior, architecture, schema, flow, or domain meaning changed.
- If no suitable note exists, create one.

Never store secret values in Obsidian.
Only document env var names.
